{title: Whiter than Snow}
{artist: James Nicholson & William Fischer}
{key: G}
{time: 3/4}
{tempo: 76}

Verse 1
[G]Lord Jesus, I [C]long to be [G]perfectly whole; I [C]want thee for[G]ever to [A]live in my [D]soul.
[G]Break down every [C]idol, cast [G]out every foe — now [C]wash me, and [G]I shall be [D]whiter than [G]snow.

Chorus
[G]Whiter than snow, yes, [D]whiter than snow —
now [C]wash me, and [G]I shall be [D]whiter than [G]snow.

Verse 2
[G]Lord Jesus, look down [C]from Thy throne in the [G]skies, And help me [C]to make a complete sacrifice; I [A]give up myself, and whatever [D]I
[G]know, Now wash me [C]and I shall [G]be whiter than snow. Whiter than snow, yes, [C]whiter than snow; Now [G]wash me, and I shall [D]be whiter than [G]snow.

Verse 3
[G]Lord Jesus, for this [C]I most humbly entreat, I [G]wait, blessed Lord, at [C]Thy crucified feet, By faith, for [A]my cleansing, I see Thy [D]blood
[G]flow, Now wash me [C]and I shall [G]be whiter than snow. Whiter than snow, yes, [C]whiter than snow; Now [G]wash me, and I shall [D]be whiter than [G]snow.

Verse 4
[G]Lord Jesus, Thou seest [C]I patiently wait, Come now, [G]and within me a [C]new heart create; To those who [A]have sought Thee, Thou never [D]said'st
[G]``No,'' Now wash me [C]and I shall [G]be whiter than snow. Whiter than snow, yes, [C]whiter than snow; Now [G]wash me, and I shall [D]be whiter than [G]snow.
